              "colSpan": 8,
              "type": "text",
              "showBorder": false,
              "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:34px;color:#E2571C;\"><b>PHONETIC SKILL 2</b></span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size:14px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#868e96;\"><b>TWO CONSONANTS FOLLOW THE VOWEL</b></span></p>",
              "fontSize": 34,
              "color": "#1a1a1a",
              "textAlign": "center",
              "verticalAlign": "center",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "underline": false,
              "richText": true,
              "lineHeight": 1.05,
              "fontFamily": "Helvetica"
            },
            {
              "id": "rh14",
              "row": 1,
              "col": 0,
              "rowSpan": 3,
              "colSpan": 8,
              "type": "text",
              "showBorder": true,
              "text": "<p><span style=\"color:#E2571C;\"><b>THE RULE:</b></span> When the vowel is followed by two consonants and nothing more, the vowel will be <b>short</b>[citation:2].</p><p><span style=\"color:#1c7ed6;\"><b>EXAMPLES:</b></span> <b>jump</b> (j-u-m-p), <b>last</b> (l-a-s-t), <b>mint</b> (m-i-n-t)[citation:2].</p><p><span style=\"color:#2d7d46;\"><b>WHY IT MATTERS:</b></span> This helps students decode CVCC and CCVC words, building on Skill 1[citation:12].</p>",
              "fontSize": 20,
              "color": "#1a1a1a",
              "textAlign": "left",
              "verticalAlign": "top",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "underline": false,
              "richText": true,
              "lineHeight": 1.12,
              "fontFamily": "Georgia"
            },
