            {
              "id": "rh20",
              "row": 1,
              "col": 0,
              "rowSpan": 3,
              "colSpan": 8,
              "type": "text",
              "showBorder": true,
              "text": "<p><span style=\"color:#E2571C;\"><b>THE RULE:</b></span> When a vowel stands alone, it will be <b>long</b>[citation:2].</p><p><span style=\"color:#1c7ed6;\"><b>EXAMPLES:</b></span> <b>go</b> (g-o), <b>I</b> (I), <b>she</b> (sh-e)[citation:2].</p><p><span style=\"color:#2d7d46;\"><b>WHY IT MATTERS:</b></span> This introduces open syllables—a key concept for multisyllabic words[citation:12].</p>",
              "fontSize": 20,
              "color": "#1a1a1a",
              "textAlign": "left",
              "verticalAlign": "top",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "underline": false,
