              "rowSpan": 3,
              "colSpan": 8,
              "type": "text",
              "showBorder": true,
              "text": "<p><span style=\"color:#E2571C;\"><b>THE RULE:</b></span> When a word ends with a silent e, the first vowel will be <b>long</b>[citation:2].</p><p><span style=\"color:#1c7ed6;\"><b>EXAMPLES:</b></span> <b>hope</b> (h-o-p-e), <b>bake</b> (b-a-k-e), <b>tune</b> (t-u-n-e)[citation:2].</p><p><span style=\"color:#2d7d46;\"><b>WHY IT MATTERS:</b></span> This is the VCe pattern—a critical long vowel pattern[citation:12].</p>",
