              "rowSpan": 3,
              "colSpan": 8,
              "type": "text",
              "showBorder": true,
              "text": "<p><span style=\"color:#E2571C;\"><b>THE RULE:</b></span> When vowels are adjacent, the second vowel is silent, and the first vowel is <b>long</b>[citation:2].</p><p><span style=\"color:#1c7ed6;\"><b>EXAMPLES:</b></span> <b>boat</b> (b-o-a-t), <b>seat</b> (s-e-a-t), <b>feel</b> (f-e-e-l)[citation:2].</p><p><span style=\"color:#2d7d46;\"><b>WHY IT MATTERS:</b></span> This covers vowel teams like ai, ea, ee, oa, and more[citation:10].</p>",
