              "row": 1,
              "col": 0,
              "rowSpan": 3,
              "colSpan": 8,
              "type": "text",
              "showBorder": true,
              "text": "<p><span style=\"color:#1c7ed6;\"><b>THE RULE:</b></span> If there is only one guardian consonant following the vowel, that consonant will move on to the next syllable[citation:3].</p><p><span style=\"color:#E2571C;\"><b>EXAMPLES:</b></span> <b>motel</b> (mo·tel), <b>program</b> (pro·gram), <b>locate</b> (lo·cate)[citation:7][citation:9].</p><p><span style=\"color:#2d7d46;\"><b>WHY IT MATTERS:</b></span> This helps students break multisyllabic words into decodable chunks[citation:3].</p>",
              "fontSize": 20,
              "color": "#1a1a1a",
              "textAlign": "left",
              "verticalAlign": "top",
              "bold": false,
