              "colSpan": 8,
              "type": "text",
              "showBorder": false,
              "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:34px;color:#1c7ed6;\"><b>DECODING SKILL 2</b></span>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size:14px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#868e96;\"><b>TWO GUARDIAN CONSONANTS SPLIT</b></span></p>",
              "fontSize": 34,
              "color": "#1a1a1a",
              "textAlign": "center",
              "verticalAlign": "center",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "underline": false,
              "richText": true,
              "lineHeight": 1.05,
              "fontFamily": "Helvetica"
            },
            {
              "id": "rh44",
              "row": 1,
              "col": 0,
              "rowSpan": 3,
              "colSpan": 8,
              "type": "text",
              "showBorder": true,
              "text": "<p><span style=\"color:#1c7ed6;\"><b>THE RULE:</b></span> When a vowel is followed by two guardian consonants, the consonants will split. The first consonant stays in the first syllable, and the second consonant moves to the next syllable[citation:3].</p><p><span style=\"color:#E2571C;\"><b>EXAMPLES:</b></span> <b>campus</b> (cam·pus), <b>extreme</b> (ex·treme), <b>explain</b> (ex·plain)[citation:9].</p><p><span style=\"color:#2d7d46;\"><b>WHY IT MATTERS:</b></span> This is the VC/CV pattern—essential for decoding longer words[citation:3].</p>",
              "fontSize": 20,
              "color": "#1a1a1a",
              "textAlign": "left",
              "verticalAlign": "top",
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "underline": false,
              "richText": true,
              "lineHeight": 1.12,
              "fontFamily": "Georgia"
            },
            {
              "id": "rh45",
              "row": 4,
              "col": 0,
              "rowSpan": 3,
              "colSpan": 8,
              "type": "table",
              "showBorder": true,
              "tableRows": 3,
              "tableCols": 8,
